        "text": "Base rate/reference class: for a two-month-ahead level forecast on JOLTS openings, a persistence/random-walk prior usually beats a strong directional call unless payrolls, hires, or layoffs show a decisive break. The latest level is 7.594 million, but the April-to-May plateau after a large March-to-April jump and softer June payroll signal argue for modest mean reversion rather than extrapolating the April surge."
