        "kind": "math",
        "text": "Prior/update/interval: persistence prior = May 2026 openings 7.594 million. Historical sample for volatility = fetched Jan-May 2026 same-series levels 7.240, 6.922, 6.887, 7.585, 7.594 million, giving monthly changes -0.318, -0.035, +0.698, +0.009. Sample sigma = 0.431 million. Adjustment components: -0.06 million for May hires falling to 5.170 million, -0.04 million for quits still low at 1.9 percent and layoffs up to 1.708 million, -0.04 million for June payroll slowing to +57,000, -0.004 rounding/level judgment, so point = 7.594 - 0.144 = 7.45 million. For a two-month horizon, half-width = 1.28 * sqrt(2) * sigma = 1.28 * 1.414 * 0.431 = 0.78 million, so 80 percent interval = 7.45 +/- 0.78 = [6.67, 8.23]."
